-- catchall.pgm - Universal Fallback Handler Component
-- Essential component for handling unrecognized input gracefully
-- This should be the LAST component loaded to serve as the ultimate fallback
-- when no other recognizer matches user input

-- The Ultimate Fallback Recognizer
-- This uses a very broad pattern that matches any single word or phrase
-- Place this at the END of your script so it only triggers when nothing else matches

Recognizer "[unrecognized]"
	Remember "User said something unrecognized: [unrecognized]"

	-- Helpful and encouraging responses
	Option Say "I'm not quite sure what you mean by '[unrecognized]'. Could you try saying it differently?"
	Option Say "I didn't understand '[unrecognized]'. Can you rephrase that for me?"
	Option Say "Hmm, '[unrecognized]' isn't something I recognize. What did you have in mind?"
	Option Say "I'm not familiar with '[unrecognized]'. Could you explain what you meant?"
	Option Say "That's interesting! I don't know about '[unrecognized]' yet. Can you tell me more?"

	-- Educational responses that guide users
	Option Say "I'm still learning! '[unrecognized]' is new to me. Try asking in a different way?"
	Option Say "I want to help, but '[unrecognized]' doesn't ring a bell. What would you like to know?"
	Option Say "Good question about '[unrecognized]'! I'm not sure about that one. Can you be more specific?"

	-- Gentle redirects with examples
	Option Say "I'm not sure about '[unrecognized]'. Try asking something like 'hello' or 'what can you do'?"
	Option Say "I didn't catch that. Maybe try 'help', 'hello', or tell me what's on your mind?"

-- Very Broad Catch-All for Multiple Words
-- This catches longer phrases that don't match any specific recognizer
Recognizer "[phrase] [more]"
	Remember "User said multi-word unrecognized phrase: [phrase] [more]"

	Option Say "I'm not quite following '[phrase] [more]'. Could you break that down for me?"
	Option Say "That's an interesting phrase! I don't understand '[phrase] [more]' yet. Can you explain?"
	Option Say "I want to help with '[phrase] [more]', but I'm not sure what you mean. Can you rephrase?"
	Option Say "Hmm, '[phrase] [more]' is beyond my current knowledge. What specifically are you asking?"

-- Even Broader Catch-All for Long Input
-- This catches very long or complex input that other recognizers miss
Recognizer "[a] [b] [c] [d]"
	Remember "User said long unrecognized input"

	Option Say "That's quite a lot to process! I'm having trouble understanding. Could you simplify?"
	Option Say "I think I'm missing something in all of that. Can you break it down into smaller pieces?"
	Option Say "That seems complex! I'd love to help, but could you ask about one thing at a time?"
	Option Say "I'm getting a bit lost in all those details. What's the main thing you'd like to know?"

-- Emergency Fallback for Unusual Characters
-- This is for when users type special characters or unusual input
Recognizer "[anything]"
	Remember "Ultimate fallback triggered"

	Option Say "I'm having trouble understanding that input. Try using simple words or phrases?"
	Option Say "Something about that didn't parse correctly. Could you try again with different wording?"
	Option Say "I'm not quite sure how to interpret that. Can you try expressing it another way?"

-- Meta-Help When User Seems Lost
-- These can be triggered by the above recognizers to provide guidance
Sequence "offer_help"
	Say "If you're not sure what to ask, try:"
	Say "• 'hello' to start a conversation"
	Say "• 'help' to learn what I can do"
	Say "• 'what can you do' to see my capabilities"
	Say "• Just tell me what's on your mind!"

Sequence "suggest_rephrase"
	Say "Here are some tips for talking with me:"
	Say "• Use simple, clear language"
	Say "• Ask one question at a time"
	Say "• Try being more specific"
	Say "• Use common words when possible"

-- Fallback Memory Patterns
-- These help the bot learn from unrecognized input
Recognizer "teach me about [topic]"
	Remember "User wants to teach me about [topic]"
	Option Say "I'd love to learn about [topic]! What should I know?"
	Option Say "Please teach me about [topic]! I'm all ears."

Recognizer "you should know [fact]"
	Remember "User suggests I should know: [fact]"
	Option Say "Thanks for teaching me that [fact]! I'll remember that."
	Option Say "Good to know about [fact]! I appreciate you sharing that."

-- Encouragement for Trying Again
Recognizer "this isn't working"
	Remember "User frustrated with interaction"
	Option Say "I understand it can be frustrating! Let's try a different approach. What would help?"
	Option Say "Sorry it's not working well! What specifically can I do better?"
	Do "suggest_rephrase"

Recognizer "you don't understand anything"
	Remember "User thinks bot doesn't understand"
	Option Say "You're right, I'm still learning! What would help me understand you better?"
	Option Say "I hear your frustration. What can I do to be more helpful?"
	Do "offer_help"
